    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "human"
      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Paulo.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 2 as a operative. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Courier With a Route</strong> — Unknown dispatcher — a delivery route that runs through Star Hill</p><p>Status: At large — last seen walking into the dark end of Star Hill's main street reading Waluigi's working notebook, satchel on, pistol discarded</p><p>A courier with a satchel, a cheap pistol, a route through Star Hill, and an issued word for what the hill had become. He shot Mr. L first, went through the clinic's front window for it, put a gun to Waluigi's face twice, and left with the one object nobody flew to Star Hill for. He never set the satchel down.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Cheap Pistol (discarded)</strong> — “A courier with a satchel, a cheap pistol, a route through Star Hill, and an issued word for what the hill had become.”</li><li><strong>Satchel Strap</strong> — “At large — last seen walking into the dark end of Star Hill's main street reading Waluigi's working notebook, satchel on, pistol discarded”</li><li><strong>Issued Word</strong> — “Couriers are issued words with routes.”</li><li><strong>The Shot</strong> — “The shot took the lip off a fallen rotor blade beside Waluigi's ear and put the archivist down; Wario threw him the notebook unopened; Paulo caught it, said 'smart', and walked away reading it — 'Now let's see what you”</li><li><strong>Walks Away Reading</strong> — “The shot took the lip off a fallen rotor blade beside Waluigi's ear and put the archivist down; Wario threw him the notebook unopened; Paulo caught it, said 'smart', and walked away reading it — 'Now let's see what you”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/paulo</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/paulo</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
